WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.730
Do we finally know where the last 2 remaining
Road Poneglyphs are that the straw hats still

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.880
need to find so they can reach laugh tale?

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:14.559
At the very least we have just gotten a few
major clues and a bunch of new information

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:15.870
dropped on our heads.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:23.470
There are 3 likely locations for it: Elbaf,
an island called Vira and Beehive Island,

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.470
Blackbeards base of operation.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.830
And, as I will explain to you, I personally
believe that Elbaf and Shanks are the most

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.689
likely candidates here.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:35.830
Now you might be like: Manu, where is this
info coming from?

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.810
There is no new One Piece chapter.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:38.940
Well, wrong!

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.940
Kind of.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.530
Even though the One Piece Manga is on a four
week break at the moment, Eiichiro Oda, the

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:48.600
author of one piece has decided to release
a series of 4 mini booklets as a small gift

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.140
to readers in every release of SHounen Jump
instead.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:58.660
This series is titled 'The Road to Laugh Tale'
and documents Oda-sensei's preparation for

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.030
the final Saga of One PIece.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:06.130
The booklet contains a lot of character sketches
and recaps of things we already know.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:12.359
However there are also some very chunky nuggets
of fresh information and reveals to be found

00:01:12.359 --> 00:01:13.359
as well.

00:01:13.359 --> 00:01:20.249
This first volume is focused very heavily
on Roger and how he became pirate king, dedicating

00:01:20.249 --> 00:01:23.109
a whole page to the mysterious Poneglyphs.

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:29.159
And by far the biggest thing in this I think,
is that Oda discusses the locations of the

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:31.109
four road poneglyphs here.

00:01:31.109 --> 00:01:35.499
We of course already know of 2 that the straw
hats have in their possession: The one from

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:41.770
Zou and one form Big Mom, that Brook heroically
made a successful rubbing off, similar to

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.729
how Roger got his hands on it.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:50.069
The third poneglyph Roger found in Wano itself
and the last one was located in Fishman island,

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:54.880
where it stood right next to Joyboys apology
letter to the mermaid princess.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.279
Now funnily enough, we didn't actually know
for a fact whether the third road poneglyph

00:02:00.279 --> 00:02:01.880
was still in wano.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.749
All we have seen so far are two of the 30+
rio poneglyphs that detail the history of

00:02:07.749 --> 00:02:08.820
the void century.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:15.770
However, this booklet tells us, that Kaido's
rule over a closed border Wano has kept anyone

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:19.450
else from getting their hands on his road
poneglyph.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.940
Which is huge in a number of ways.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:27.390
Because I think it's basically the first time
we officially get confirmed that it's still

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:32.460
waiting here in wano for the straw hats to
find.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.300
That means that the straw hats will get their
hands on it.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:41.460
It also means we still have another story
thread that needs to happen in Wano, which

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:46.960
makes me happy, because I didn't want to leave
the country as quickly as the last few chapters

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.250
made it seem.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:57.490
However, it also means, that other people
might now come for that very same road poneglyph.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:01.430
Im thinking of course Blackbeard, and for
some reason now also Buggy.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.220
Luffy's two main rivals to becoming pirate
king.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:10.450
Because Blackbeard surely would have been
aware of Kaido sitting on top of that particular

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.450
red stone.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:16.530
It also might be the reason or at least one
of the reasons why Momo decided to leave Wano's

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:22.680
borders closed for now until Luffy reaches
Laugh Tale, telling Zuneshia, 'thanks for

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.840
dropping by, but actually could you come back
another time?'

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:31.860
The fact that a road poneglyph is located
in wano also adds a lot more weight to the

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:39.390
reveal that Oden's father and Momo's grandfather,
Kozuki Sukiyaki, former Shogun of Wano and

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:43.150
heir of the Kozuki clan is still alive.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:49.350
I somehow totally overlooked that in the last
chapter, but he was obviously the one who

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:53.180
taught Oden how to read and write the language
of the ancient kingdom.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:04:00.160
In other words, Oda just snuck another character
back into the story that can potentially lead

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.390
the way to the final island.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.840
This is HUGE.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.930
Sukiyaki might be the lottery ticket someone
like Blackbeard has been waiting for to make

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.319
his way to Laugh tale as well, should he not
get his hands on Robin.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:22.620
Him and Robin are pretty much the only two
confirmed people alive who can do this.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:27.440
And should Blackbeard make his way to wano
to get this poneglyph and find out who SUkiyaki

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:33.320
is, that would be a true advantage falling
into his hands.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:40.389
But as if this wasn't enough, Oda-sensei also
decided to tease us with the location of last

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:44.490
remaining, lost road poneglyph that used to
be on Fishman island.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:50.290
And he gives us 3 possible locations: Elbaf,
Beehive island itself and Vira.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:55.139
You might now be asking what the Usopp is
a Vira.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:05:00.070
It's actually an island that was named by
Nami once, very early on in the story as she's

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.630
reading Noland's journnal.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:07.110
In other words, it's an island that was visited
by Noland 400 years ago and was described

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.870
as a very lively and happy place.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:15.820
Since then, this small town expanded into
a full-blown country, but it was no longer

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:19.440
a happy place to live.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:25.290
Instead it was ruled by a tyrannical government
associated with the world nobles.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:31.740
After the breakout of a rebellion, it was
finally freed by the revolutionary army.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:38.070
Oda-sensei of course mentions that there are
other possibilities for the location, as he

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:43.340
should, but he still chose to focus on these
three specifically.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:48.860
And I think it makes sense, because all 3
of these islands seem to have ties to powerful

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.830
people who might have gotten their hands on
the last poneglyph.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:59.600
Vira is connected to the Revolutionaries and
Dragon, who clearly know quite a lot about

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:05.250
the true history, which was why Robin in particular
got send to them by Kuma.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:10.169
Maybe it's the island the revolutionaries
moved their operations to, after they got

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.010
raided by Bladckbeards crew on their old base.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:18.830
And who knows, maybe blackbeard came for them
exactly because he knew that they had a road

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:19.870
poneglyph.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.350
Which of course brings us to Beehive island.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:27.790
It used to be the base for Rocks D Xebec,
who also has a page dedicated to him in this

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:32.900
booklet, that details his connections to Blackbeard,
who also named his ship the Xebec.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:38.790
Now it's Blackbeards home and since Blackbeard
is also aiming to become pirate king, it would

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:48.710
make sense for him to already have his hands
on a poneglyph there as well.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.980
Lastly, there is Elbaf.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:55.760
Not only has elbaf been hinted at over and
over again to be the next island the straw

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:00.360
hats will travel to after wano, as I've discussed
in previous videos, you have Usopps relationship

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:05.370
to the giants, Big mom's relationship to the
giants, the introduction of Loki, and so on.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:10.060
But it also seems like Elbaf has strong ties
to another Yonko.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:11.060
Shanks.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:16.680
As I explained in his character analysis,
Shanks has a very strong viking theme going

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:17.680
on.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.580
There is of course his ship, that has the
same style as Sorry and Broggy's, but Shanks

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:28.030
is also inspired by the Nordic God Tyr, who
also lost an arm to a beast and a number of

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.130
other parallels.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:33.870
We also know that the Yonko, including Shanks
hold territory.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:37.120
Again something that is discussed in the Road
to Laugh Tale.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.639
Territorial dispute in the new world between
the Yonko and co.

00:07:40.639 --> 00:07:46.750
And so I have always been a strong supporter
of the idea that Elbaf is part of Shank's

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.750
territory.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.169
His home turf in the new world if you like.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.949
A man with a bounty of over 4B berries.

00:07:52.949 --> 00:07:56.830
I have 61 Million berries, 100 for each subscriber.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.830
Ouch.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:02.060
But we're not trying to beat Shanks, we're
trying to beat Trebol, who has 99M for the

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:06.630
magical 100M berries, in other words 1M subscribers.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:12.620
So not only can you make that dream come true
by subscribing, but you also get freshly harvested

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.009
one piece content, every single week.

00:08:15.009 --> 00:08:19.860
And I think it would truly make sense for
the man who is making sure to carry on Roger's

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:26.490
will as a Yonko, to grab the most easily accessible
road poneglyph from Fishman island and protect

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.630
it for only the right person to see.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.180
The man Roger was waiting for.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:35.159
In other words Luffy.

00:08:35.159 --> 00:08:40.779
Shanks definitely knew about the Road poneglyph
there, he traveled to fishman island with

00:08:40.779 --> 00:08:41.779
Roger.

00:08:41.779 --> 00:08:47.500
Elbaf is a true fortress of an island, just
like Wano, filled with some of the most powerful

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.790
warriors in the entire world.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:54.860
So really what better place to have the final
road potnglyph hidden, than the next location

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:57.020
the straw hats are heading to.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.720
A place where luffy can finally meet shanks.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:04.520
A place where he has to earn his right to
the last red stone and proof his worth as

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.520
a YOnko.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.340
And also a place, where finally Shanks and
Blackbeard face each other once again, as

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:14.010
Blackbeard would surely come for that very
same poneglyph as well.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:18.300
And if you really want to know what has been
foreshadowed about Elbaf and how the arc might

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:23.760
play out in the end and why Shanks has such
strong ties to nordic mythology, you should

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:26.550
not miss out on these two videos right here.

